/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
 * Atlas Drill — Brazil
 *
 * Two drill sets sharing one map, one projection, and one gesture layer:
 *   - States: the 26 states plus the Federal District, answered by naming
 *     or by tapping the actual shape.
 *   - Cities: every state capital, plus the commercial hub wherever that's
 *     a different city (Espírito Santo, Santa Catarina), answered by
 *     naming or by tapping a point within a distance-based allowance.
 *
 * Geometry: Natural Earth 1:50m admin-1, filtered to Brazil, simplified
 * offline and embedded below.
 *
 * Elevation: a real DEM -- ETOPO 10-arc-minute global relief, sampled over
 * Brazil, contoured into four bands (200/500/800/1100 m) and clipped to
 * these same state outlines. 10 arc-minutes is ~18 km per cell, so summits
 * average down (Pico da Neblina reads ~2190 m against its true 2995 m, and
 * nothing in-country clears 1800 m at this resolution, which is why there
 * is no 2000 m band). Mean elevation over this outline computes to 326 m
 * against a published ~320 m -- a useful check that the grid is registered
 * to the country correctly. Every value is measured, not estimated.
 *
 * No runtime fetch, no map library, no browser storage.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

